// ------------------------------------------------------------- printing ----

// A Lua string is a BYTE string, so lua-to-llvm-ir.abnf holds one host character
// per byte: every code unit is 0..255. print writes those bytes raw (js_luaprint);
// js_luaout decodes them as UTF-8 for the message of an uncaught error, which
// leaves as text through fail(). A byte that starts no valid sequence is passed
// through as its own code point, which is what utf8.DecodeRune's (RuneError, 1)
// answer makes the Go twin do.
//
// luChar is BYTE-IDENTICAL to swift-rt.metajs's js_char, and deliberately not
// shared: lib/runtime.metajs's own js_char has a different contract (the {__char}
// box). Keep the two texts in step by hand.
